Subject: Modeling Algorithms - BRepGProp_Gauss refines U to the requested precision, as it refines L
Upstream: https://github.com/Open-Cascade-SAS/OCCT/issues/1675 (BRepGProp_Gauss never refines U; a PR needs OCCT's CLA)
Applies to: OCCT V7_9_3, after 0003 (which changes BRepGProp_Face.cxx only; this patch is
     against the pinned BRepGProp_Gauss.cxx).
Why: BRepGProp_Gauss::Compute with an Eps (BRepGProp::VolumeProperties and SurfaceProperties
     with an eps, Silico's precise measure) never refines U: EpsU starts at 0 and is set only
     in a branch the U loop can't reach, so the loop ends after its first pass, and U is
     integrated once, at SIntOrder(eps) points on each span UKnots gives. U's error is also
     left out of the estimate (ErrUL is set only on the first L order's pass). So an
     extruded two-span B-spline measured 9.4e-4 low and its swept face's area 0.27% high,
     a slanted prism of a one-span B-spline (the stress test's) 5.2% low in area, B-spline
     surfaces' areas up to about 1e-5 off, and one NIST part's volume 3.6e-5 off, each
     with an estimate of about 1e-16. This patch computes U's error on both L orders'
     passes, refreshes it on every U pass, and sets EpsU from the requested precision and
     the strip's value by L's rule (EpsL = 0.9 * |DDim * eps|), so U subdivides until it
     meets eps or the subdivision cap, whose branch (EpsU = ErrorU, break) ends it. Setting
     EpsU alone isn't enough: U would refine on the first L order's pass only, and the two
     L orders would disagree by U's error. The default integration (Compute without an
     Eps, FreeCAD's) is a different function and is unchanged to the bit.
Moves: tests/determinism/oracle-reference.json's summary hashes of 117 of its 208 cases (the
     list is in the PR), to be re-recorded with the maintainer: volumes by at most 1.8e-13
     relative, areas not at all, centres of mass by at most 8.6e-9 (3.9e-10 of the shape's
     size); not their measures, B-reps, meshes, or histories. No committed fingerprint
     (every golden checks unchanged), and not the stress reference (default integration).
Drop when: an OCCT release refines U in BRepGProp_Gauss::Compute's Eps path (check that
     EpsU can become nonzero before the U loop's first pass ends), or when
     extruded_bsplines.rs passes with the patch removed.

--- a/src/BRepGProp/BRepGProp_Gauss.cxx
+++ b/src/BRepGProp/BRepGProp_Gauss.cxx
@@ -769,7 +769,7 @@
                       BRepGProp_Gauss::Inertia aLocal[2];
 
                       Standard_Integer       iUS     = URange[kU];
-                      const Standard_Integer aLength = iGLEnd - iGL;
+                      const Standard_Integer aLength = iGLEnd;
 
                       const Standard_Real um = 0.5 * (U2->Value(iUS) + U1->Value(iUS));
                       const Standard_Real ur = 0.5 * (U2->Value(iUS) - U1->Value(iUS));
@@ -819,6 +819,10 @@
                         anUI.Iyy = mult(aLocal[0].Iyy, ur);
                         anUI.Izz = mult(aLocal[0].Izz, ur);
                       }
+
+                      // U's error, on every L order's pass.
+                      if (iGLEnd == 2)
+                        ErrU->Value(iUS) = mult(Abs(aLocal[1].Mass - aLocal[0].Mass), ur);
 
                       if (iGL > 0)
                         continue;
@@ -862,10 +866,18 @@
                     }
                   }
 
-                  if (JU == iUSubEnd)
+                  if (JU >= iUSubEnd)
                   {
                     kUEnd  = 2;
                     ErrorU = ErrU->Value(ErrU->Max());
+                    if (iGLEnd == 2)
+                    {
+                      // U's tolerance from the requested one and the strip's value, as L's.
+                      Standard_Real aStrip = 0.0;
+                      for (i = 1; i <= JU; ++i)
+                        aStrip += anInertiaU->Value(i).Mass;
+                      EpsU = 0.9 * Abs(aStrip * anEpsilon);
+                    }
                   }
                 } while ((ErrorU - EpsU > 0.0 && EpsU != 0.0) || kUEnd == 1);
 
